<!DOCTYPE softwarelist SYSTEM "softwarelist.dtd">
<!--
license:CC0-1.0

No original NCR 9010 boot disk is known to survive.  These system disks
were reconstructed: the system image is taken from the SYSGEN programs
OS1.COM / OS.COM (SYSGEN 1.2 with a built-in SB-80 2.60), the disk layout
from the SBIOS 1.8 and NCRGEN sources and the boot ROMs 1023/1024.  They
add the Digital Research tools PIP, STAT, ED, ASM, LOAD, DDT and DUMP
(Lifeboat edition) and the FORMAT and COPY utilities written for this
reconstruction (sources on the disks).

Disk format: cylinder 0 side 0 FM 26 x 128 bytes with the "NCR FMT-" ID
block (type 07 = double sided double density), all other tracks MFM
26 x 256 bytes; the system lives on cylinders 72 and 73, side 0.
-->
